## 3. The orphan-queue mechanism: what drives it, and does it need a live runtime?

**Driver: a signal-driven (SIGCHLD) hook that runs on the runtime&#39;s park path. It requires a live runtime. There is no background thread and no spawned task.**

```rust
// src/runtime/process.rs:11-43  (entire file)
/// Responsible for cleaning up orphaned child processes on Unix platforms.
#[derive(Debug)]
pub(crate) struct Driver {
    park: SignalDriver,
    signal_handle: SignalHandle,
}

impl Driver {
    pub(crate) fn new(park: SignalDriver) -&gt; Self { ... }

    pub(crate) fn park(&amp;mut self, handle: &amp;driver::Handle) {
        self.park.park(handle);
        GlobalOrphanQueue::reap_orphans(&amp;self.signal_handle);   // line 33
    }

    pub(crate) fn park_timeout(&amp;mut self, handle: &amp;driver::Handle, duration: Duration) {
        self.park.park_timeout(handle, duration);
        GlobalOrphanQueue::reap_orphans(&amp;self.signal_handle);   // line 38
    }

    pub(crate) fn shutdown(&amp;mut self, handle: &amp;driver::Handle) {
        self.park.shutdown(handle);      // &lt;-- NOTE: no reap_orphans here
    }
}
```

The queue state and the SIGCHLD registration:

```rust
// src/process/unix/orphan.rs:41-44
pub(crate) struct OrphanQueueImpl&lt;T&gt; {
    sigchild: Mutex&lt;Option&lt;watch::Receiver&lt;()&gt;&gt;&gt;,
    queue: Mutex&lt;Vec&lt;T&gt;&gt;,
}
```

```rust
// src/process/unix/orphan.rs:79-110
pub(crate) fn reap_orphans(&amp;self, handle: &amp;SignalHandle)
where
    T: Wait,
{
    // If someone else is holding the lock, they will be responsible for draining
    // the queue as necessary, so we can safely bail if that happens
    if let Some(mut sigchild_guard) = self.sigchild.try_lock() {
        match &amp;mut *sigchild_guard {
            Some(sigchild) =&gt; {
                if sigchild.try_has_changed().and_then(Result::ok).is_some() {
                    drain_orphan_queue(self.queue.lock());
                }
            }
            None =&gt; {
                let queue = self.queue.lock();

                // Be lazy and only initialize the SIGCHLD listener if there
                // are any orphaned processes in the queue.
                if !queue.is_empty() {
                    if let Ok(sigchild) = signal_with_handle(SignalKind::child(), handle) {
                        *sigchild_guard = Some(sigchild);
                        drain_orphan_queue(queue);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Characteristics, all visible in the above:

- **Global, not per-runtime.** A `static ORPHAN_QUEUE` (`src/process/unix/mod.rs:67-83`), shared across all runtimes in the process.
- **Lazy SIGCHLD registration** — the listener is only registered on the first park *after* an orphan is pushed. Confirmed by test `does_not_register_signal_if_queue_empty` (`orphan.rs:296-316`).
- **Non-blocking** — a `try_lock` bail at `orphan.rs:85` means concurrent drains are skipped rather than serialized.
- **Best-effort by design** — if the signal driver is gone, registration fails and nothing is reaped:
  ```rust
