<h1>Plan: Suppress LNK4099 Noise + Gate the Release Upload on Local Verification</h1>
<h2>Problem</h2>
<p>Two independent defects in <code>just release</code>, both surfaced by the Windows MSVC cross build:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Linker noise.</strong> The static MSVC CRT <code>.lib</code> files reference debug-info PDBs at a Microsoft-internal path (<code>D:\a\_work\1\s\binaries\...</code>) that are never distributed. <code>cargo-xwin</code> fetches the <code>.lib</code> files but not those PDBs, so <code>lld-link</code> emits ~60 <code>LNK4099 &quot;Cannot use debug info&quot;</code> lines per link. rustc's <code>linker_messages</code> lint is <strong>on by default</strong> and promotes linker stderr to a Rust warning, so this floods every Windows build's output for all developers, not just Linux cross-builders. The linked binary is unaffected — this is missing debug info only, with no effect on codegen, correctness, or the shipped artifact.</p>
