<tr><td>Missing debug files</td><td>none referenced</td><td>~40 CRT PDB references → LNK4099</td></tr>
<tr><td>Lint fires</td><td>no</td><td>yes, ~60 lines</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<p>So the answer to your original instinct — &quot;I write Rust and never see these&quot; — is that on Linux the linker has nothing to complain about. Everything in your Linux link is either locally compiled or a system <code>.so</code>, and none of it carries a CodeView pointer to a file on a CI machine in Redmond.</p>
<p>The real asymmetry isn't Rust-vs-other-languages, it's <em>self-hosted debug info vs foreign prebuilt debug info</em>. You hit it only now because MSVC is the first target where your build graph contains code you didn't compile.</p>
