<div class="entry entry-assistant" id="entry-283"><div class="label">Assistant</div><p>Fair — I answered a different question. Yours is: <em>why doesn't Microsoft rebuild the CRT without the path, given the GUID is what matters?</em></p>
<p>I don't know, and I should have said that instead of circling around format requirements, which is the wrong reason.</p>
<p>The likely answer is that stripping the path would require a build step after compilation that rewrites every object's debug record — and the <code>.lib</code> archive format doesn't make that easy. But that's speculation. A rebuilt-from-scratch CRT using a different debug format would sidestep it entirely, and I don't know whether that's been tried or why it hasn't shipped.</p>
<p>What I can verify is whether current MSVC has a flag for it. <code>link /PDBALTPATH</code> only rewrites the path at link time, not in the <code>.lib</code>.</p>
