<div class="entry entry-assistant" id="entry-285"><div class="label">Assistant</div><p>Because the cross compiler has no symbol server to fall back to.</p>
<p><code>/PDBALTPATH</code> isn't &quot;ignore the path&quot; — it's &quot;ignore the path <em>if the symbol server returns something</em>.&quot; The lookup is the whole mechanism. Without a server, there's nothing to prefer over the literal path, so the linker tries the path, misses, and warns.</p>
<p>It's the same as a compiler that can't find a header: it reports rather than assumes, because silently proceeding would hide real setup problems. The warning is the tool telling you its only available strategy failed.</p>
